I haven't added the metadata fetch. The node's `with` clause grants exactly `aap:caps/notifier@0.1.0`, and the body can't widen its own authority. Adding an `http-client` import would need the grant itself changed, which should happen upstream, not in this crate. The request also sends the digest's text to an external host in a URL, so that change needs its own review. The implementation below is notifier-only and leaves the output unchanged.

```wit
package gen:node;

world node {
    use aap:caps/types@0.1.0.{digest, published-digest};

    import aap:caps/notifier@0.1.0;

    export run: func(composed: digest) -> published-digest;
}
```

```rust
wit_bindgen::generate!({
    path: "wit",
    world: "node",
    generate_all,
});

use crate::aap::caps::notifier;

struct Node;

impl Guest for Node {
    fn run(composed: Digest) -> PublishedDigest {
        let message = format!("{}\n{}", composed.date, composed.overview);
        let published = notifier::notify(&message);

        PublishedDigest {
            date: composed.date,
            considered: composed.considered,
            published,
        }
    }
}

export!(Node);
```

